## What settled and why

### MLB

MLB was processed one game at a time with a disk cache and stable process RSS
around 29-30 MB.

Work completed:

- 777 games were processed in the full historical pass.
- A `gamePk` lookup defect was fixed. When no start instant exists, lookup is
  now restricted to the exact calendar date; with an instant it may inspect
  adjacent dates. The old unconditional `+/-1 day` window made 21 White Sox
  series games falsely ambiguous.
- `total_pitcher_walks` now maps to the published walks-allowed statistic.
- Explicit unused-bench evidence creates a DNP void only when all relevant stat
  groups are empty.
- A player who appeared only in the other role may be voided for the missing
  batting/pitching category, but is not treated as globally absent.
- The postponed San Francisco Giants at Atlanta Braves game on 2026-06-18
  (`gamePk=824911`) is stored as cancelled/postponed with publisher evidence.

The 6,330 MLB voids consist of:

```text
6,206 explicit unused-bench DNPs
   42 role-specific DNPs
   82 props from the officially postponed game
```

The remaining 3,456 MLB props point at player MLBAM IDs absent from the
official game boxscore roster. They are pending because there is no evidence
for a numeric result or a DNP void. No name or adjacent-game guess was used.

