## Settlement behavior repaired

The principal code changes in this session were:

- `settlement/settle_game.py`
  - every early return now accounts for all open props as pending;
  - sourced cancellations void idempotently before a live fetch;
  - missing event linkage is reported as missing durable publisher identity.
- `settle_props.py`
  - future games are excluded by default;
  - `--through` provides an explicit historical boundary;
  - `--max-games` bounds a run.
- `settlement/mlb_api.py` and `mlb_settle.py`
  - serial disk-cached fetches, pacing/retries, exact `gamePk` lookup,
    walks mapping, and evidence-backed DNP handling.
- `settlement/mls_settle.py`
  - DB-first provider-separated settlement, exact fixture identity,
    RotoWire attempted passes, deep markets, and durable DNP voids.
- `settlement/ufc_settle.py`
  - corrected finish semantics and cancellation visibility.
- `settlement/wc_settle.py`, `repair_world_cup_results.py`,
  `ingest_wc_logs.py`, and `ingest_soccer_logs.py`
  - missing data no longer masquerades as DNP; stable athlete IDs are preferred.
- `ingest_fotmob_soccer_logs.py`
  - exact match-date appearance rosters disambiguate duplicate names;
  - unresolved rows can be safely repaired without overwriting resolved IDs
    with null.
- `migrate_schema.py`
  - durable `cancelled_at`, `cancel_reason`, and `cancel_source` fields.
- Migration and identity-spine test fixtures were updated so both new numbered
  migrations and the RotoWire provider table are explicitly covered.

The predictions multi-sport migration was concurrent pre-existing worktree WIP;
this session preserved it and updated the synthetic migration fixtures so the
combined current schema is testable.

